# [RIFT](../wg/rift.html)

## Summary

The RIFT working group met at IETF 127 in San Francisco. The session covered working group document status, key-value (KV) store extensions for IP address block allocation, SRv6 extensions for RIFT, and an updated proposal for RIFT multicast routing.

## Key Discussion Points

### Working Group Status and Document Updates
Jeff Tantsura presented the [Chairs slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rift-chairs-slides-00). Key updates included:
* **RFC Publication:** RFC 9592 (RIFT Key-Value Data Store Structure) was published.
* **Working Group Drafts:**
  * `draft-ietf-rift-auto-evpn`: The draft has expired. The authors need to refresh it and request an early review to prepare for Working Group Last Call (WGLC).
* **Individual Drafts:** Presentations scheduled for address block extensions, SRv6 extensions, and multicast.

