### RIFT Extensions for SRv6
Weiqiang Cheng presented [02-RIFT extensions for SRv6](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rift-02-rift-extensions-for-srv6-00).
* **Overview:** Details extensions to enable SRv6 (including compressed SID / cSID support and Zero Touch Provisioning) in RIFT networks.
* **Updates since IETF 117:**
  * Added variable-length encoding for SRv6 KV information.
  * Defined a dedicated SRv6 locator element.
  * Added use cases for AI backend networks and hyperscale data center WAN/front-end networks.
  * Added references to compressed SID (RFC 9800) support.
  * Clarified per-publisher unique Key IDs to avoid KV collisions across publishers.
* **Core Extensions:**
  * SRv6 ZTP via KV distribution of locators, END SIDs, and adjacency END.X SIDs from controller/Top-of-Fabric (ToF) nodes.
  * SRv6 locator advertisement (northbound propagation and southbound positive/negative disaggregation tags).
  * SRv6 adjacency SIDs in neighbor elements.
* **Discussion & Adoption Request:** Weiqiang Cheng requested WG adoption for the draft. Jeff Tantsura acknowledged the request and indicated that chairs will initiate review for adoption.

