### RIFT Multicast
Jeffrey Zhang presented [RIFT Multicast](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-rift-rift-multicast-00).
* **Overview:** Updated the specification for RIFT multicast after resolving issues around subtree connection algorithms.
* **Mechanism:**
  * Operates similarly to Bidirectional PIM without an explicit Rendezvous Point (RP).
  * Nodes send tree-specific northbound joins up to top-of-fabric/sub-top nodes.
  * Sub-tree roots at the top layer run a hash algorithm to choose a candidate root and advertise child nodes via southbound TIEs (Topology Information Elements).
  * When topology changes occur, sub-tree roots select the designated root based on child counts and system ID tie-breakers, reparenting as needed.
  * Supports multi-plane topologies where east-west connections synchronize top-layer topology and tree state.
* **Discussion:**
  * Sandy Zhang and Christian Hopps asked questions regarding receiver-side mechanics and offered to provide feedback on the list.
  * In response to an attendee's question about inter-DC multicast, Jeffrey Zhang clarified that the protocol applies within a RIFT domain, while inter-DC traffic would interface via protocols like PIM or EVPN at the domain boundary.

